\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The dictionary of Figure~\ref {fig:dictionary}, mirrored. The same five hypotheses serve as load-bearing regularity routes for the \emph  {binary} ($n{=}2$) fundamental equation of information (Cauchy relative at rational weights; unique regular solution is the concave Shannon entropy), and vestigial when a continuum of weights makes the operative equation the continuous-coefficient~\eqref  {eq:star}. For $n{>}2$, Fischer~(1972) showed no regularity is needed (see \S  \ref {ssec:load-bearing}).}}{16}{}\protected@file@percent }
